# Text files are stored and checked out with LF, everywhere.
#
# This is not cosmetic. requirements.txt was committed with CRLF, so on the
# Linux CI runner the last line read `vllm\r` -- and the filter that was
# supposed to drop it, `grep -v '^vllm$'`, matched nothing while still exiting
# 0. CI silently installed the multi-GB CUDA serving stack the filter existed
# to keep out, and the whole job failed before a single test ran. The shell
# scripts under scripts/ run on Linux too, and would break the same way.
* text=auto eol=lf
